<section class="why" aria-labelledby="why-title">
  <div class="container inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">Why Moonlit</p>
    <h2 id="why-title" class="section-title">Plugins you can trust with your release credentials.</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article>
        <div class="text">
          <h3>Deny by default</h3>
          <p>
            A plugin with no <code class="inline-code">permissions</code> block gets zero capabilities.
            Grants are explicit and per plugin.
          </p>
        </div>
        <pre class="snippet"><span class="k">permissions</span>:
  <span class="k">network</span>: [<span class="s">"api.github.com"</span>]
  <span class="k">exec</span>: [<span class="s">"git"</span>]</pre>
      </article>
      <article>
        <div class="text">
          <h3>Outputs flow forward</h3>
          <p>Every step publishes namespaced outputs. Later steps read them with one expression syntax.</p>
        </div>
        <pre class="snippet"><span class="k">branch</span>: $(<span class="f">output:repo:branch</span>)
<span class="k">version</span>: $(<span class="f">output:version:nextFullVersion</span>)
<span class="k">project</span>: $(<span class="f">vars:projectPath</span>)
<span class="k">token</span>: $(<span class="f">GITHUB_TOKEN</span>)</pre>
      </article>
      <article>
        <div class="text">
          <h3>Pulled like images</h3>
          <p>
            Plugins ship over OCI, from registry.moonlit.rs or any compliant registry. Write them in any
            language that targets WASI Preview 2.
          </p>
        </div>
        <pre class="snippet"><span class="k">url</span>: <span class="s">"oci://registry.moonlit.rs/</span>
<span class="s">      wolfware/semantic-release:1.0.0"</span>
<span class="c"># or your own registry</span>
<span class="k">url</span>: <span class="s">"oci://ghcr.io/acme/notify:0.3.1"</span></pre>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

